/*! \mainpage Laser People Detection

  \section Introduction 

  Algorithm for people detection from horizontal range laser sensors scans, 
  - based on Adaboost to classify legs,
  - uses a previous trained classifier stored in a txt file (data/classifierData/boostFile.txt)
     - see algorithm labrobotica/algorithms/laser_people_train for training,
     - note that the current boostFile.txt files are the result of training with a Hokuyo UTM-30LX laser. Using other devices for detection with different features (resolution mainly) may need new training.
  - receives scan data, does a segmentation and feature extraction of each segment,
  - classifies each segment as leg or not, and makes groups pairing legs,
  - and outputs final person positions.

  This algorithm has a wrapper for ROS called \b iri_laser_people_detection.
  There is also a visual-tool ROS node for labeling called \b iri_laser_people_label.

  \section Contents
  - \link installation Installation \endlink
  - \link use          Use          \endlink
  - \link doc          Doc          \endlink
  - \link faq          FAQ          \endlink
  .

